      "text": "Bogotá – Pereira, Salento and the Cocora Valley"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "c8e977fed5fa8f2e13e37b8662d94f1eabb1af6c3483926b4d2f1fd080bce998",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-work-mw9nvgw6-cx25ndvy",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, transfer to the airport and fly to Pereira.\n\nOn arrival, head to the Cocora Valley in Los Nevados National Park. After a welcome drink, a specialist guide will introduce you to the valley’s natural landscape and its best-known feature, the wax palms.\n\nThe world’s tallest wax palms grow here. The wax palm is Colombia’s national tree. Its resin was once used to make candles, which gave the palm its name. These palms grow at elevations above 3,000 metres in the Andes, and around 2,000 trees remain.\n\nOptional activities during the visit include horseback riding and planting a palm seedling.\n\nYou can have lunch at a restaurant in the valley. **Lunch is not included in the price.** Another option is to try your hand as a barista and make coffee at Café Jesús Martín in Salento.\n\nAfter the valley, head to Salento, a small town with brightly painted houses, quiet streets and artisans’ workshops. You’ll walk through the town centre and up to a viewpoint overlooking the valley and the surrounding green slopes.\n\nTransfer to and check in at **Movich Hotel de Pereira**."
    },
